<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Slavs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Slavic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Slavs are a large group of peoples of central and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> speaking Slavic languages. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">medieval period</a> Slavic groups settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, as accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> note. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a> describe Slavic tributaries and trade along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> routes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/slavs.jpg" alt="Slavs" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CrazyPhunk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slavic_europe_(Kosovo_shaded).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
